#!/usr/bin/env python3
# session-closeout -- canonical weight-session close-out device (DGN-388)
#
# Two jobs, one instance-side helper (stdlib only: sys, os, sqlite3, argparse,
# subprocess -- the last one only to call the framework's pin owner API):
#
#   1. VALIDATOR (--check): decide whether the LATEST weight session is
#      "properly closed" = has a non-NULL session_type_id AND >=1 workout_sets
#      row. Used by routines/rx-gen.sh BEFORE it emits a normal rotation rx, so
#      an un-closed session (untagged and/or setless) can never be silently
#      rotated past. This is the device that would have caught sessions 44/45.
#
#   2. CLOSE-OUT (default action): finalize a session by writing
#      workouts.session_type_id for a given session id + session_type code.
#      kit_life.py / kit_life.sh are FRAMEWORK code and must NOT be hand-patched,
#      so the tag write is a direct, idempotent sqlite3 UPDATE encapsulated
#      here -- this is the ONE canonical close-out write path. The helper also
#      reports whether the session carries workout_sets rows (warns if 0).
#
# Usage:
#   session-closeout <session_id> <session_type_code> [--db PATH]   # close out
#   session-closeout --check [--db PATH]                            # validator
#   session-closeout --exercise-exit <session_id> <exercise> [--reason TEXT]
#
# Close-out also retires the 표3 종목카드 from the shared dashboard.md pin
# (DGN-967 `--pin-clear workout`) -- best-effort, --no-pin-clear opts out.
#
# 2026-08-25 (session 10092 boundary defects). Three additions, each with its
# own commented rationale block further down:
#   D1  the session marker SWEEP -- .reply-pending above all, whose survival
#       past this close-out deadlocked the next session's fast path 31/31.
#   D4  the ZERO-MINUTE GATE -- a session with minutes=0/kcal=0 is REFUSED
#       before any write, never silently booked as zero.
#   D5/D6 the CLOSE-OUT CARD and the EXERCISE EXIT RESOLUTION -- stdout is now
#       a renderable artifact, and no closed session leaves a dangling `[ ]`.
#
# CHANNELS (changed 2026-08-25): stdout of a CLOSE-OUT is the CARD. The operator
# log ("session N has M rows", SWEPT..., PIN_CARD...) moved to stderr, so
# `session-closeout ... 2>&1` reads exactly as it did before. --check is
# unchanged: its OK / NEEDS_CLOSEOUT line is still stdout (rx-gen parses it).
#
# Default DB: <this dir>/../../database/kit_life.db
#
# Validator exit codes:
#   0 = latest weight session properly closed (or no weight sessions) -> proceed
#   3 = latest weight session NEEDS close-out (stdout: "NEEDS_CLOSEOUT <id> <date>")
# Sweep (--sweep, the CRON's full-mode entry point) exit codes:
#   0 = always. stdout: SWEEP_NONE / SWEEP_SKIP <id> <why> / SWEEP_CLEAN <id> /
#       SWEPT <id> rc=<n> <reasons>. See do_sweep for what it may and may not do.
# Close-out exit codes:
#   0 = session tagged (idempotent; already-correct is a no-op success)
#   1 = error (unknown session id / unknown session_type code / bad args)
#   4 = REFUSED, nothing written: the session has no duration/energy (D4).
#       stdout carries "CLOSEOUT_REFUSED unmeasured <id> <date>" plus the exact
#       `kit_life.sh workout-upd` line that fixes it.
#   5 = --exercise-exit only: the card's table could not be built, so the card
#       was refused rather than degraded into prose.

